{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed807260302/14/codegen_prompts/4.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/14`\n- 题号：`4`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed807260302/14/4.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"4\">\n- `description`：将网格中每个L形三格标记视为\"折叠指令\"，沿其拐角处的轴线将相邻的矩形色块面板折叠翻转，覆盖到另一侧。\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中有若干互不重叠的实心矩形色块（每个色块是单一前景色的实心矩形，颜色各不相同）。在某些色块的边缘外侧，紧贴着一个由maroon像素组成的L形标记（恰好三个像素构成直角L形，占据2x2区域中的三格）。L形的拐角像素紧邻色块边缘的某个位置，L形的两臂分别沿色块边缘方向和垂直于边缘方向延伸。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对于每个L形标记，确定其拐角像素所贴靠的色块边缘（上、下、左、右）。\n  - L形的一臂沿边缘方向延伸，标出折叠轴在边缘上的位置；另一臂垂直于边缘向外延伸，指示折叠方向。\n  - 以折叠轴为镜像线，将色块中位于轴线一侧（L形垂直臂所指的反方向一侧）的部分镜像翻转到轴线的另一侧（L形垂直臂所指方向）。翻转后的像素覆盖在背景上，若覆盖位置已有其他前景色则保持被覆盖色不变（先到优先）。\n  - 原色块中被折叠过去的那部分像素保留在原位不消失。\n  - 所有L形标记在输出中被擦除为背景色。\n- `Key insight`：L形标记同时编码了两个信息——折叠轴的位置和折叠方向——需要拆解其几何结构才能正确执行折叠操作，而不是简单的镜像翻转整个色块。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：eval/88e364bc, train/3cd86f4f, eval/b10624e5, train/bae5c565, eval/21897d95, eval/6e4f6532, train/5adee1b2, train/11dc524f\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"88e364bc\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3389\nmechanism=0.3940\nlexical=0.0121\ncode_feature=0.5714\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:rotation, object:closed_region, object:grid_edge, object:marker, object:rectangle, relation:adjacent, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/88e364bc.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/88e364bc.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide yellow pixels inside walled regions in the direction dictated by border-legend arrows.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color; yellow pixels sit inside enclosed regions bounded by colored walls.\n- Border legends: small rectangles on the grid edge whose fill color C matches a region's border color. Each legend contains a center dot and an indicator dot encoding a direction.\n\nRule:\n- For each enclosed region, identify its border color C and look up the legend with fill color C.\n- The direction from the legend's center dot to its indicator dot gives the slide direction.\n- All yellow pixels in that region slide in that direction, stacking against the far wall.\n\nKey insight: Legend fill color links to region border color; the center→indicator offset encodes the movement vector.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Yellow pixels inside colored-border regions move in the direction indicated by the red pixel in the legend with matching background color, stopping at region boundary.\",\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"yellow pixels inside colored-border regions s\",\n  \"dst\": null,\n  \"match_cond\": \"\",\n  \"path\": \"move(s, direction=legend.red_pixel_offset) where legend.background_color == s.containing_region.border_color until s.touches(region_boundary)\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"legend on grid edge with background color C and red pixel indicates: yellow pixels in regions with border color C move in direction from blue center to red pixel\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"legend/control-pixels\",\n    \"region-membership\",\n    \"directional-movement\",\n    \"boundary-collision\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"3cd86f4f\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3363\nmechanism=0.4319\nlexical=0.0130\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:rotation, object:grid_edge, object:rectangle, operation:reflect, relation:adjacent, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/3cd86f4f.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/3cd86f4f.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nShear the rectangular input down-left onto a black canvas.\n\nInput structure\nA rectangular grid of colored pixels with no internal empty region to infer.\n\nRule\nCreate a black output with the same height and width W + H - 1, then copy\neach input row r unchanged starting at column H - 1 - r.\n\nKey insight\nThe colors and row contents are preserved; only the row offsets change so\nthe left edge forms a descending diagonal.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"symmetry/pattern\",\n  \"src\": \"the full input rectangle, interpreted as rows to be diagonally staggered\",\n  \"dst\": \"black canvas with the same height and enough columns for the staggered rows\",\n  \"transform\": \"copy every row unchanged; place row r starting at column H - 1 - r so adjacent rows shift one column left downward\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"same height, width W + H - 1\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"b10624e5\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2528\nmechanism=0.2801\nlexical=0.0116\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:rotation, operation:reflect, relation:adjacent, relation:direction, relation:overlap, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/b10624e5.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/b10624e5.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nReplicate a motif across quadrants with scaling and reflection keyed to red anchor blocks.\n\nInput structure:\n- Grid divided into four quadrants by a full-row and full-column divider of a single non-bg color.\n- Each quadrant contains a red (2) square anchor block of varying size.\n- The top-left quadrant also has a colored motif attached to its red anchor.\n\nRule:\n- Use the top-left quadrant's motif as the source pattern.\n- For each other quadrant, scale the motif by the ratio of that quadrant's red block size to the source red block size.\n- Reflect horizontally for right-side quadrants, vertically for bottom quadrants (both for bottom-right).\n- Align the scaled/reflected motif so its red region overlaps the target anchor, then stamp non-bg pixels.\n\nKey insight: Red block size encodes the scale factor; quadrant position encodes the reflection axes.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Copy the pattern adjacent to the red anchor block in the top-left quadrant to other quadrants, scaling and reflecting based on the relative size and position of matching red anchor blocks.\",\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"colored pixels adjacent to the red anchor block in top-left quadrant s\",\n  \"dst\": \"positions adjacent to red anchor blocks in other quadrants d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.anchor_color == d.anchor_color (both red); scale_factor = d.red_block.size / s.red_block.size; reflection determined by quadrant relationship\",\n  \"path\": \"\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"keep source\",\n  \"transform\": \"scale(s, factor=d.red_block.size/src_red_block.size) and reflect(s, axis=quadrant_relative_axis)\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": null,\n  \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: identify red anchor blocks in each quadrant; Step 2: compute scale factor from red block size ratios; Step 3: determine reflection axis from quadrant positions (horizontal for left-right, vertical for top-bottom); Step 4: copy scaled and reflected pattern to each target quadrant anchored at its red block\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"scaling\",\n    \"reflection\",\n    \"quadrant-based symmetry\",\n    \"anchor matching\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"bae5c565\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2747\nmechanism=0.3707\nlexical=0.0128\ncode_feature=0.1667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, object:grid_edge, object:marker, operation:reflect, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/bae5c565.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/bae5c565.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nErase the top palette row and redraw it below as a widening wedge centered on its missing cell.\n\nInput structure\n- The top row is a palette row with exactly one background gap.\n- Below it, the only foreground is one vertical marker bar of a single color.\n- The marker bar is either in the gap column or immediately beside it.\n\nRule\n- Clear the grid to background.\n- Starting at the top of the marker bar, each next row copies one more\n  column of the top-row palette on both sides of the gap.\n- Fill the gap column with the marker color, and keep the vertical marker bar.\n\nKey insight\n- The lone background cell in the top row is the center of the expanding\n  copy; the lower vertical bar provides the center color and the row where\n  the expansion begins.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"symmetry/pattern\",\n  \"src\": \"top palette row with one bg gap and a lower single-color marker bar\",\n  \"dst\": \"widening wedge rows below the marker bar, centered on the top-row gap\",\n  \"transform\": \"erase the top row; in each row from the marker top downward, copy the top-row colors within the current centered interval, replace the gap column with the marker color, and keep the marker bar\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"21897d95\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2513\nmechanism=0.2778\nlexical=0.0118\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:rotation, object:marker, object:rectangle, relation:adjacent, relation:direction\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/21897d95.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/21897d95.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRepaint regions from T-shaped control markers, erase the markers, and optionally rotate based on a color-9 L-marker.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
