/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/1/code.py:158:    Pull the nearest reachable maroon pixels into the 3x3 block around the lone red center, filling that block by columns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/1/code.py:165:    - Flood-fill outward from passable cells adjacent to the target through floor and maroon cells; only reachable maroons are eligible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/1/code.py:166:    - Rank eligible maroons by BFS distance, breaking ties by row then column, erase the closest ones from their source positions, and place them into the target in column-major order from the top-left.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/1/code.py:167:    - Any destination cells beyond the number of moved maroons keep their original green/red colors, and unreachable maroons stay in place.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/1/code.py:170:    - The walls still determine which maroons can be harvested at all, but this variant is identified by the destination pattern: it fills downward through the left column before moving to the next column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/21897d95/D14/2/code.py:317:    \"\"\"Find a 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker and return its corner position.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D16/1/code.py:20:     interiors, maroon head lines and matching maroon destination lines.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/21897d95/D2/0/code.py:317:    \"\"\"Find a 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker and return its corner position.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/21897d95/D2/0/code.py:359:    - A 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker controls rotation: ┐ (corner top-right) means rotate 90 degrees CCW, and ┌ (corner top-left) means rotate 90 degrees CW.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D6/2/code.py:3:# Change: 1:1 — 每个容器恰好对应一条目标线，颜色相同（均为maroon/9）... → 颜色匹配配对\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D6/2/code.py:23:# - The only semantic change is that head/destination markers are no longer globally maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D7/1/code.py:20:#   containers, grey/orange interior, and a maroon head-line flush with one container side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D7/1/code.py:21:# - Movers still have a same-shaped maroon destination line farther along the head direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D7/1/code.py:25:#   for a matching maroon line above it and move upward by min(distance, 3). In the variant,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D7/1/code.py:42:# - The fix is to treat only non-border-adjacent maroon components as external destinations.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D7/1/code.py:74:# - Heads must remain the only maroon pixels adjacent to their own border.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/2/code.py:32:#     - 原题通过容器外侧相邻的 maroon 头线确定方向\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/2/code.py:35:#       而是在同一轴的两侧各放一个候选 maroon 目标线；轴由目标线对给出，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/2/code.py:44:#       - reachability still depends only on flood-fill through floor/maroon cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/2/code.py:45:#       - maroons are still ranked by distance, then row, then column\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/2/code.py:54:#     - source maroons are placed only on reachable floor cells, never in destination or wall cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/2/code.py:55:#     - distractor maroons are placed only on unreachable floor cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/2/code.py:65:#     - generate_input() preserves both conditions and also guarantees k >= 4 reachable maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/2/code.py:105:    Move the closest reachable maroon pixels into the 3×3 block around the unique red center using a spiral fill.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/2/code.py:108:    - Orange floor cells hold scattered maroon tokens, and magenta walls may carve corridors around the target.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/2/code.py:112:    - Flood-fill outward from passable cells touching the destination; reachable maroon tokens are the movable candidates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/2/code.py:114:    - Erase those source maroons back to floor and write them into the destination along a clockwise outer-to-inner spiral.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/2/code.py:117:    - Connectivity still decides which maroons qualify, but the visible change is the write path: partial fills trace the destination's perimeter before reaching the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/2/code.py:177:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == 9)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/2/code.py:178:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < inf]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/2/code.py:179:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/2/code.py:181:    k = min(len(fill_order), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D4/2/code.py:182:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/21897d95/D2/1/code.py:19:#   L-shaped color-9 rotation marker.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/21897d95/D2/1/code.py:327:    \"\"\"Find a 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker and return its corner position.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D7/3/code.py:30:      * no_head decoy: the border+interior exists, a distant maroon target line\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D7/3/code.py:31:        exists on one side, but the 1-cell-thick maroon line adjacent to the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D7/3/code.py:34:        maroon head/dest lines.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D7/3/code.py:51:      maroon markers, preventing ambiguous head/destination pairing.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/21897d95/D10/0/code.py:342:    \"\"\"Find a 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker and return its corner position.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/21897d95/D2/3/code.py:297:    \"\"\"Find a 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker and return its corner position.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D3/1/code.py:9:#   containers, gray interior cells, one 1-cell-thick maroon head line on a container side,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D3/1/code.py:10:#   and an aligned maroon destination line farther along the motion axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D3/2/code.py:64:  - 仍然只使用 magenta 背景、黑框容器、灰/橙内部和 maroon 标记，图面层次简单。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/21897d95/D2/2/code.py:25:#     - optional L-shaped color-9 rotation cue\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/21897d95/D2/2/code.py:317:    \"\"\"Find a 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker and return its corner position.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:9:#     original_dd6b8c4b: reachable maroon cells are ranked by floor BFS distance; unreachable maroons stay put.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:20:#     blocked maroons: placed in side pockets so they are clearly unreachable by floor BFS but adjacent to the wall network.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:23:#       - a maroon in the top pocket is unreachable from the destination, so it simply remains in the top pocket.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:25:#       - the same maroon first attaches to the adjacent magenta wall cells,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:27:#       - if that slot is an inner opening next to the destination, the maroon becomes reachable and can be selected into the 3x3 block,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:28:#       - if that slot is an outer opening on the outer frame, the maroon stops there and remains visible in the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:30:#       - D18 changes only the handling of originally unreachable maroons; reachable-source ranking and destination filling stay as in the seed task.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:33:#     - pockets are only one cell each, so each moved maroon has a single unambiguous origin.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:34:#     - generator enforces both branches: at least one blocked maroon moves to an inner opening and at least one moves to an outer opening.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:37:#       - \"unreachable maroons can be ignored for selection\" is no longer safe.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:38:#       - clearing only chosen reachable maroons is no longer sufficient because blocked maroons now relocate before ranking.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:39:#       - BFS only on floor+maroon still works for final selection, but it must run after the wall-motion stage.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:41:#       - blocked maroons must touch at least one wall cell; generator guarantees this by using pocket cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:43:#       - no two blocked maroons may need the same opening; generator validates distinct nearest targets.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:45:#     - destination, inner ring, outer frame, pocket connectors, openings, and maroons are all placed on fixed non-overlapping cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:46:#     - reachable source maroons are sampled only from floor cells that are not pockets and not opening slots.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:48:#     - the only new visual event is \"sealed-pocket maroons jump to wall gaps\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:206:def _move_blocked_maroons(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:227:    maroons = [(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:228:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:229:    for r, c in maroons:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:264:    Move blocked maroon pixels to the nearest wall opening, then fill the center block with the closest reachable maroons.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:268:    - Magenta walls form an inner ring, an outer frame, and small sealed side pockets containing some maroon pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:271:    - First, any maroon already reachable from the destination through floor/maroon cells stays in place.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:272:    - Any maroon trapped behind the magenta walls instead travels along the connected wall framework to the nearest open side-center slot.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:273:    - After that relocation, recompute reachability and move the closest reachable maroons into the 3x3 destination in row-major order, erasing them from their source cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:276:    - The critical change is not how reachable maroons are ranked, but that blocked maroons are no longer static distractors: the wall network itself routes them to visible openings, and inner openings can turn them into new candidates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:288:    staged, _ = _move_blocked_maroons(grid, cr, cc, dest_cells, FLOOR_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:291:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(staged == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:292:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < 10**9]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:293:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:295:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:296:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:338:    staged, moved = _move_blocked_maroons(np.asarray(grid, dtype=int), CENTER_R, CENTER_C, dest_cells, FLOOR_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:340:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(staged == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:341:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < 10**9]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:342:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:343:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[: min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:379:    staged_probe, moved_probe = _move_blocked_maroons(probe, CENTER_R, CENTER_C, dest_cells, FLOOR_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D18/2/code.py:411:    staged, moved = _move_blocked_maroons(inp, CENTER_R, CENTER_C, dest_cells, FLOOR_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d8e07eb2/D12/1/code.py:219:# -- Fixed repeated-color scaffold --\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D3/3/code.py:30:#     - Output synthesis in the generator must mirror this exact local rewrite.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a6f40cea/D10/1/code.py:597:    # Place L-shaped components in random corners\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/21897d95/D11/0/code.py:349:    \"\"\"Find a 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker and return its corner position.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/21897d95/D11/0/code.py:384:    - An optional 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker is embedded inside one region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a6f40cea/D10/2/code.py:243:    - Monochrome components still create solid stripes or L-shaped Manhattan links between their mapped touch points.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/21897d95/D8/0/code.py:323:    \"\"\"Find a 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker and return its elbow orientation.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:23:#      maroon tokens. Output still moves the closest reachable maroon tokens\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:27:#      old: 3x3 block -> cap 9 -> 12 reachable maroons still fill only 9 cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:28:#      new: 4x4 block -> cap 16 -> the same 12 reachable maroons fill 12 cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:29:#      new: 4x4 block + 19 reachable maroons -> only the closest 16 move, 3 stay.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:34:#      reachable maroons remain outside once the square is full.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:55:#      fill completely while nearby reachable maroons remain on the floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:59:#    - Walls remain outside the square; maroons remain on floor cells, so layers\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:68:#      overflow cases (reachable maroons > capacity) so the D6 change is active.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:175:    Move the closest reachable maroon pixels into a variable-size square container marked by a red corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:178:    - Orange floor contains optional magenta walls and scattered maroon (9) pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:182:    - Flood-fill outward from passable cells touching the square, traversing only floor and maroon cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:183:    - Sort reachable maroon pixels by BFS distance, then by row and column, and move as many as fit into the square in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:184:    - Moved maroons are erased back to floor; any extra reachable or unreachable maroons remain where they are.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:187:    - The red pixel is no longer the center of a fixed 3x3 target. The solver must first recover the full red/green square, because its area determines how many maroons can be collected.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:198:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:199:    maroons = [item for item in maroons if item[0] < 10**9]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:200:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:202:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/0/code.py:203:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d8e07eb2/D11/0/code.py:35:#       - place a 5-pixel L-shaped marker in the bottom-right corner\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d8e07eb2/D10/2/code.py:53:#    Object placement stays on the original 30x22 fixed scaffold. Table cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:19:      - orange floor, optional magenta walls, maroon movable tokens\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:21:      - reachability is still decided by 4-connected flood-fill through floor/maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:22:      - each container still fills in row-major order using its closest assigned maroons\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:26:      - a maroon reachable from both containers is assigned to the nearer container\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:40:      sources: maroon cells placed on floor cells owned by one of the two containers\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:41:      distractors: optional maroon cells unreachable from both containers\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:46:      - sort all reachable maroons by that one distance\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:50:      - for each maroon, compare the two distances and assign the maroon to the nearer block\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:51:      - inside each block, sort only that block's assigned maroons and fill its own 3x3 cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:53:      - if a central maroon can reach both blocks, the old solver would have no notion of competition\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:70:    - original single BFS distance map assumes every reachable maroon belongs to the same target; invalid now\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:71:    - original `chosen = maroons[:k]` assumes one global quota; invalid now because each block needs its own quota\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:78:      - chosen maroon sources and distractors are sampled from floor cells only\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:85:      - at least one moved maroon comes from such an overlap region, so multi-target ownership is exercised\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:181:    Route reachable maroon pixels into multiple 3×3 destination blocks around red centers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:184:    - bg = orange floor, optional magenta walls, scattered maroon (9) pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:188:    - For each destination block, compute reachability through floor/maroon cells, stopping at walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:189:    - Every reachable maroon is assigned to the nearest destination block; equal distances go to the earlier center in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:190:    - Inside each block, assigned maroons are ranked by distance to that block and fill the block in row-major order; moved maroons are erased back to floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:211:    owned_maroons = [[] for _ in containers]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:217:        owned_maroons[owner].append((int(dists[owner][r, c]), r, c))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:220:        owned_maroons[idx].sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/1/code.py:221:        chosen = owned_maroons[idx][: len(dest_cells)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/21897d95/D8/1/code.py:387:    \"\"\"Find a 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker and return its grid quadrant.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a6f40cea/D11/0/code.py:30:#     - this variant upgrades each L-component into one connected outside scaffold with four\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a6f40cea/D11/0/code.py:56:#     - the new outer scaffold stays strictly outside the frame except for isolated ring-touch\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/21897d95/D7/1/code.py:310:    - There is no separate L-shaped rotation sprite; the total number of T markers is the only rotation cue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/2/code.py:64:#    - Assumption: at least one passable floor/maroon cell touches the container so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/2/code.py:92:    Move the closest reachable maroon pixels into the irregular green container attached to the unique red anchor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/2/code.py:95:    - The board still uses orange floor, optional magenta walls, and scattered maroon tokens.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/2/code.py:99:    - Maroon pixels that can reach the container through floor/maroon cells are candidates, with walls blocking traversal exactly as before.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/2/code.py:100:    - Rank reachable maroons by BFS distance to the container, then place the closest ones into the container's own cells in row-major order, skipping positions outside the shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/2/code.py:101:    - Any moved maroon source is erased back to floor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/2/code.py:153:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == 9)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/2/code.py:154:    maroons = [t for t in maroons if t[0] < inf]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/2/code.py:155:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/2/code.py:157:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D6/2/code.py:158:    chosen = {(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1818057f/D12/0/code.py:16:#      globally mirror-symmetric, some are almost symmetric but have one extra spur.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1818057f/D12/0/code.py:22:#      complete footprint is not mirror-symmetric, the entire blob disappears.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1818057f/D12/0/code.py:152:    Keep only mirror-symmetric foreground components and recolor them teal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1818057f/D12/0/code.py:157:    - Some components are exact mirror-symmetric as whole shapes; others are slightly lopsided.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1818057f/D12/0/code.py:161:    - If a component has at least one horizontal or vertical mirror axis, recolor the entire component to teal (8).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1818057f/D12/0/code.py:164:    Key insight: The decision is global per component, not local per pixel. A blob survives only when its complete footprint matches itself under some mirror reflection.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a6f40cea/D4/2/code.py:61:#   the interior, while the L-shaped completion from another object clearly terminates\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a6f40cea/D7/0/code.py:18:#  