central 3×3 block and leave teal transport trails behind.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:156:    - The canvas uses orange floor, magenta walls, scattered maroon tokens, and a fixed green 3×3 target with one red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:157:    - Floor openings beside the target connect into corridors; only maroons reachable through those corridors participate.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:160:    - Flood-fill outward from passable cells touching the target, treating orange floor and maroon tokens as passable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:161:    - Sort reachable maroons by flood-fill distance, then by row and column; the closest ones fill the target in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:162:    - Each chosen source maroon disappears back to orange, and every orange floor cell on its discovered route to the target is recolored teal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:181:    maroons = [(int(dist[r, c]), int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(grid == MAROON)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:182:    maroons = [item for item in maroons if item[0] < 10**9]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:183:    maroons.sort()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:185:    k = min(len(dest_cells), len(maroons))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:186:    chosen = [(r, c) for _, r, c in maroons[:k]]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a6f40cea/D7/1/code.py:19:#    L-shaped rectangular traces instead of only 2-3 components. Each outside\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/62593bfd/D5/2/code.py:24:      horizontal mirror image (`np.fliplr` of the cropped object patch)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/62593bfd/D5/2/code.py:34:    - New visible difference: every output object is mirrored left-right\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ce