eshi/code/21897d95/D7/2/code.py:10:#   corner (\"┌\") means an up-down mirror. The L marker is still erased into its host region\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/21897d95/D7/2/code.py:14:#   12x16 and is mirrored horizontally instead. This changes both the output geometry and the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/21897d95/D7/2/code.py:17:#   still a single, visually legible mirror operation rather than a larger rule family. To keep\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/21897d95/D7/2/code.py:18:#   the difference observable, the generator rejects L9 cases where the mirrored output would be\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/21897d95/D7/2/code.py:33:#   markers, which makes left-right and up-down mirror directions distinguishable in a few examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/21897d95/D7/2/code.py:35:#   a horizontal mirror target; if it sees `top_left`, it expects a vertical mirror target. The\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/21897d95/D7/2/code.py:292:    \"\"\"Find a 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker and return its corner position.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/21897d95/D7/2/code.py:337:    Recolor mosaic regions from T controls, erase the control shapes, and optionally mirror the finished picture from a color-9 L marker.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/21897d95/D7/2/code.py:348:    - If a color-9 L marker is present, apply a whole-grid mirror after all recoloring: ┐ (corner at top-right) means horizontal flip, ┌ (corner at top-left) means vertical flip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/21897d95/D7/2/code.py:351:    - The T geometry explains the recoloring, and the L geometry only chooses the final mirror direction; the two mechanisms stay independent until the last step.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/21897d95/D7/2/code.py:376:# L9 mirror marker\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/21897d95/D7/2/code.py:377:L9_PROBABILITY = 0.5                        # chance of placing a mirror trigger\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/21897d95/D7/2/code.p