ace base at (0,0) and place the mirrored input plug elsewhere with\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D11/1/code.py:73:#     - plug masks are thin and asymmetric, making the mirror visually obvious in\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b3084d4/D4/3/code.py:424:    plain = FEATURE in (\"plain_split\", \"mirror_sym\", \"rot_sym\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b3084d4/D4/3/code.py:429:    if FEATURE == \"mirror_sym\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b3084d4/D4/2/code.py:424:    plain = FEATURE in (\"plain_split\", \"mirror_sym\", \"rot_sym\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b3084d4/D4/2/code.py:429:    if FEATURE == \"mirror_sym\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9aaea919/D4/0/code.py:18:#    - input: left red lane has two maroon sprites, green lane has one blue sprite.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9aaea919/D4/0/code.py:20:#    - variant output: green lane keeps its bottom blue sprite, and the two newly filled slots above are maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D8/1/code.py:9:#      2. off-legend markers, usually two 3-pixel L corners on one bbox diagonal, sometimes a solid 2x2 block\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/0/code.py:21:#    {(8,8),(7,8),(9,8),(8,7),(8,9)}=1. Sprite hits and lone bg landings stay maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/0/code.py:25:#    least one lone bg landing, so each sample contains both a blue cross and a maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/0/code.py:45:#    least one maroon lone landing in the same sample makes the branching rule inferable:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/0/code.py:46:#    one projectile on empty bg -> maroon point, multiple projectiles on empty bg -> blue\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/0/code.py:53:#    Only two effect colors remain relevant: maroon for lone bg hits / hit sprites, blue for\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/0/code.py:145:    - A landing on an existing sprite recolor