/D19/0/code.py:36:#   overwrite maroon hit sprites, so hit recoloring happens after safe recoloring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D19/0/code.py:42:#   To keep the new recolor rule readable, initial sprite colors exclude grey (5) and maroon (9),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D19/0/code.py:50:#   Only three output marker colors carry meaning: grey=safe shooter, maroon=hit sprite or lone bg\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D19/0/code.py:54:#   main() now assumes any component it recolors grey or maroon is a valid 3-cell triangle detected\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D19/0/code.py:129:    - Any sprite that is hit by at least one projectile is recolored maroon (9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D19/0/code.py:132:      maroon (9) for a single projectile.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D19/0/code.py:136:      states: safe shooters become grey, while struck sprites become maroon.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D3/2/code.py:50:#      mirroring, or hidden metadata.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D19/1/code.py:18:#     - each sprite is still a monochrome 3-pixel L or V component\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D19/1/code.py:21:#     - a shared empty-bg landing still becomes blue(1); a lone landing is maroon(9)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D19/1/code.py:23:#     - original: start from the input grid, keep all untouched sprites, recolor a hit sprite as a 3-pixel maroon object\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D19/1/code.py:59:#   - The variant uses only the original two projectile colors in the output: maroon(9) for lone landings / sprite hits, blue(1) for multi-projectile bg collisions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D19/1/code.py:128:      a hit on any sprite cell becomes maroon (9), a lone empty-bg landing becomes maroon (9),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D13/0/code.py:32:#    where a bridge cell touches the frame/control scaffold, goes out of bounds, or fails to align.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D13/0/code.py:340:    scaffold = np.full((int(H), int(W)), int(bg), dtype=int)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D13/0/code.py:344:            scaffold,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D13/0/code.py:357:        scaffold[int(ctrl_r), int(col)] = int(color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D13/0/code.py:359:    out = scaffold.copy()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D13/0/code.py:360:    old_semantics = scaffold.copy()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D13/0/code.py:373:            if int(scaffold[int(r), int(c)]) != int(bg):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D13/0/code.py:386:    inp = scaffold.copy()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D19/2/code.py:10:#     - Hit sprites still recolor solid maroon; empty landing cells still become maroon/blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D19/2/code.py:53:#     - `main()` assumes inputs still contain isolated monochrome 3-pixel L/V components.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D19/2/code.py:141:    Fire projectiles from 3-pixel triangle sprites; hit targets turn maroon while survivors get a border.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D19/2/code.py:149:    - If a landing cell lies on a sprite, the entire hit sprite becomes maroon (9). If the landing cell is empty bg, then a lone projectile paints maroon (9) and a multi-projectile collision paints blue (1).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D19/2/code.py:152:    Key insight: Orientation still determines where each projectile goes, but now the output splits sprites into two visible classes—solid-maroon victims versus original-color survivors outlined by a fixed halo.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D3/1/code.py:111:    - Away from the legend, each active marker color appears either as two L-shaped corner markers on one bbox diagonal or as a solid 2x2 blo