ral rectangles whose mirrored output differs from the raw sprite\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D4/3/code.py:55:#       - reject cases where mirrored output equals the old \"paste-as-is\" output\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D4/3/code.py:65:#     3. mirror the sprite before pasting, with the axis chosen by strip orientation + half\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D4/3/code.py:77:#     there plus a small helper to choose the mirror axis from the destination slot.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D4/3/code.py:91:    \"\"\"Return 'h' for left-right mirror and 'v' for top-bottom mirror.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D4/3/code.py:110:    Fill the template cavities with outside sprites, but mirror each sprite according to slot position.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D4/3/code.py:118:    - Match outside sprites to the hole rectangles by exact bbox cover, then mirror each sprite before insertion.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D4/3/code.py:119:    - In a vertical strip, upper-half slots use a left-right mirror and lower-half slots use a top-bottom mirror; for a horizontal strip, rotate that rule with the strip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D4/3/code.py:122:    - The placement search is unchanged from the original puzzle: only the final write step changes, because each matched slot tells you which mirror to apply.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D4/3/code.py:475:    \"\"\"Build the input grid: template frame with holes plus raw, unmirrored sprites.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D4/3/code.py:500:    \"\"\"Count branch coverage and how many pieces truly change under the mirror rule.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D4/3/code.py:517:    \"\"\"Single attempt: sample layout, build raw sprites, mirror them in output, verify with solver.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D2/2/code.py:240:    - A ray that hits