/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D9/2/code.py:29:    output: the upper original payload becomes grey, the lower mirrored copy stays blue,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D9/2/code.py:37:  original pixels from generated mirror pixels. Each generated grid contains\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D9/2/code.py:44:  - Reflection loops write mirrored pixels with the source color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D9/2/code.py:45:    This still holds; the mirrored copy should remain original-colored.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D9/2/code.py:50:  - Isolated-red handling mirrors all adjacent same-color components touched in 8-neighborhood.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D9/2/code.py:52:    recolor set after mirroring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D9/2/code.py:56:  the mirrored copy and restoring grey originals back to their payload color. Groups are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D9/2/code.py:73:  The color rule is fixed and repeated: original payload -> grey (5), mirror -> keep\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D9/2/code.py:79:  - Payload colors must not already be grey, otherwise source-vs-mirror would collapse.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D9/2/code.py:314:    mirror = {(int(2 * axis_r - r), int(c)) for r, c in source}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D9/2/code.py:317:        mirror = _transform_rows(mirror, axis_r)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D9/2/code.py:326:        \"mirror\": mirror,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D9/2/code.py:338:    mirror = {(int(r), int(2 * axis_c - c)) for r, c in source}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D9/2/code.py:341:        mirror = _transform_cols(mirror, axis_c)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D9/2/code.py:350:        \"mirror\": mirror,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D9/2/code.py:360:    mirror = {(int(2 * extent - r), int(2 * extent - c)) for r, c in s