/1/code.py:431:    colored = spr[\"payload\"] | spr[\"mirror\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D16/1/code.py:437:def _erase_mirror(canvas: np.ndarray, spr: dict, bg: int) -> None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D16/1/code.py:439:    h, w = spr[\"mirror\"].shape\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D16/1/code.py:440:    canvas[r0 : r0 + h, c0 : c0 + w][spr[\"mirror\"]] = int(bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D16/1/code.py:492:        footprint = spr[\"payload\"] | spr[\"mirror\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D16/1/code.py:504:        _erase_mirror(inp, spr, bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a32d8b75/D1/0/code.py:19:#     - Each cavity is exactly one dihedral transform (rotation / mirror) of the same 3x3 unit sprite.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a32d8b75/D1/0/code.py:36:#     - At least one cavity per legend uses a non-identity transform; mirrored variants are strongly favored.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a32d8b75/D1/0/code.py:53:#     - The output shows those silhouettes filled by rotated / mirrored colored copies, which is a direct\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a32d8b75/D1/0/code.py:263:    - Read the unit sprite, enumerate its rotations and mirrors, and match those transformed silhouettes to every enclosed cavity in the plaque.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D14/0/code.py:307:    - The projectile lands exactly 5 cells from the apex. Landing on a sprite recolors that whole sprite to maroon (9); multiple projectiles on the same empty background cell paint it blue (1); a single projectile on empty background paints it maroon (9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/291dc1e1/D6/3/code.py:51:#   template. Transformations only mirror/rotate the whole grid, preserving\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D15/2/code.py:153:    - If the landing cell belongs to another sprite, repaint that whole struck sprite maroon (9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D15/2/code.py:154:    - If the landing cell is empty background, paint it maroon (9), except when multiple projectiles share that empty cell, in which case it becomes blue (1).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D13/0/code.py:8:#    to add a missing mirrored copy onto background. For D13 we keep the same marker\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D13/0/code.py:25:#    - The original \"eligible(...)\" + write mirrored pixel assumes the reflected cell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D14/2/code.py:267:    - Within one firing step, hitting a sprite recolors that whole sprite to maroon (9); two shots that reach the same currently empty background cell make that cell blue (1); one shot on a currently empty background cell makes it maroon (9). Later steps do not repaint cells that are no longer background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/abc82100/D6/3/code.py:56:#   encoded the one-way mapping directly, so the variant must add the mirrored\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D13/1/code.py:69:    - red row -> mirror across that row\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D13/1/code.py:70:    - red column -> mirror across that column\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D3/0/code.py:351:        mirror = [(-int(r), -int(c)) for r, c in rel]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D3/0/code.py:352:        all_coords = rel + mirror + [(0, 0)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/abc82100/D6/2/code.py:32:#         maroon(9) -> red(2)    -> orange(7)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/abc82100/D6/2/code.py:34:#     - Example legend: pink source 6, maroon target 9, anchor on the teal stencil.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/abc82100/D6/2/code.py:37:#         all translated stencil cells become maroon(9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/abc82100/D6/2/code.py:39:#         (8,8)       distance 0 -> maroon(9)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D13/0/code.py:24:#      so blue collision marks, maroon hit marks, orange backgroun